BT 0.28 0.33 0.39 rg /F2 7.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 807.89 Tm (NEXUS HMS USER MANAGEMENT AND SECURITY GUIDE) Tj ET
0.12 0.39 0.65 RG 1 w 54 798.89 m 541.28 798.89 l S
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 775.89 Tm (Deactivate users promptly when employment ends, access is compromised, or a device is lost. Revoke) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 761.89 Tm (active mobile devices. Preserve audit records according to hotel retention policy rather than) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 747.89 Tm (deleting evidence.) Tj ET
BT 0.08 0.16 0.27 rg /F2 15 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 712.89 Tm (3. Roles and least privilege) Tj ET
0.12 0.39 0.65 RG 1.3 w 54 706.89 m 130 706.89 l S
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 686.89 Tm (Use role names that map to real responsibilities:) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 665.89 Tm (- Platform admin: tenants, subscriptions, modules, plugins, global password policy, and global) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 651.89 Tm (  security.) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 630.89 Tm (- Tenant admin: tenant users, local IP rules, hotel configuration, and permitted workflows.) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 609.89 Tm (- Manager: approvals, dashboards, reports, and operational oversight.) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 588.89 Tm (- Front desk: guests, reservations, check-in, stay, and checkout.) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 567.89 Tm (- Department operator: only the operational module needed by the department.) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 546.89 Tm (- Finance or HR specialist: sensitive finance or personnel operations.) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 525.89 Tm (- Read-only/reporting: view and export only what policy permits.) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 504.89 Tm (Review role assignments at least quarterly and after every organizational change. Avoid giving) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 490.89 Tm (platform scope to a user who only needs one property's operational access.) Tj ET
BT 0.08 0.16 0.27 rg /F2 15 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 455.89 Tm (4. Authentication controls) Tj ET
0.12 0.39 0.65 RG 1.3 w 54 449.89 m 130 449.89 l S
BT 0.12 0.39 0.65 rg /F2 11.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 421.89 Tm (Access and refresh tokens) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 402.89 Tm (Access tokens authenticate normal API requests. Refresh tokens are separately signed and should be) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 388.89 Tm (stored only in an appropriately protected client store. On logout, the client must remove stored) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 374.89 Tm (tokens. If a refresh token is suspected to be compromised, follow the session invalidation and secret) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 360.89 Tm (rotation procedure.) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 339.89 Tm (Production operations must provide matching `REDIS_PASSWORD` and credential-bearing `REDIS_URL`) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 325.89 Tm (secrets for the cross-replica Socket.IO adapter. The Kubernetes API reads `REDIS_URL` from a Secret,) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 311.89 Tm (while Redis reads `REDIS_PASSWORD` from the same Secret. NetworkPolicies permit Redis ingress only) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 297.89 Tm (from API pods and deny Redis egress. Redis and web pods run explicitly as non-root without privilege) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 283.89 Tm (escalation.) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 262.89 Tm (For real production, prefer managed Redis on a private network with TLS and use `rediss://`. The) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 248.89 Tm (Redis service included with Compose and Kubernetes requires authentication but does not enable TLS;) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 234.89 Tm (do not treat its internal `redis://` connection as encrypted. Redis supports realtime packet delivery) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 220.89 Tm (only; authorization remains enforced by the API and Redis is not a shared authorization cache or) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 206.89 Tm (durable audit/event store.) Tj ET
BT 0.12 0.39 0.65 rg /F2 11.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 177.89 Tm (MFA enrollment) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 158.89 Tm (1. The user opens Security and chooses MFA setup.) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 137.89 Tm (2. The server generates a TOTP secret and eight backup codes.) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 116.89 Tm (3. The QR data and codes are returned for one-time enrollment display.) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 95.89 Tm (4. The database stores encrypted values, not plaintext secrets.) Tj ET
